1
00:00:01,320 --> 00:00:02,300
Hello there!

2
00:00:05,780 --> 00:00:07,320
It's so hot!

3
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:09,420
I'm gonna burn to death!

4
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:14,360
I don't see any of us dying from these
temps, but I hope I don't overheat.

5
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:16,600
We'll be okay, right?

6
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:19,380
This is all because of that sheer pervert?

7
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:21,070
It's true.

8
00:00:21,153 --> 00:00:23,417
Heavy's letter is the reason
we're here in the first place.

9
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:24,917
We came here to track him down.

10
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,477
I must leave you and go see to a
personal matter, but fear not comrades!

11
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:32,997
I shall rejoin you as soon as
my errand is taken care of.

12
00:00:33,080 --> 00:00:34,057
P .S.

13
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:36,937
Take care of yourselves and of
course your footwear This letter

14
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:39,697
must mean that he's headed for
the Scorching Sand Stratum,

15
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:40,610
doesn't it?

16
00:00:40,693 --> 00:00:45,017
Probably based on how he acted yesterday
Then it would be best if we followed him,

17
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:45,930
right?

18
00:00:46,013 --> 00:00:47,577
I personally don't care at
all that much about Heavy,

19
00:00:47,660 --> 00:00:49,777
but I'd like to check up on
the Scorching Sand Stratum.

20
00:00:49,860 --> 00:00:51,417
So it's fine by me if we go!

21
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:52,897
So, there you have it.

22
00:00:52,980 --> 00:00:55,457
And here we are in the
scorching sand stratum.

23
00:00:55,540 --> 00:00:58,777
Now I'd better do something before
everyone melts in this intense heat.

24
00:00:58,860 --> 00:01:01,625
I'll turn on my temperature
regulation feature.

25
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:05,897
Oh, things just cool
down a lot. Thanks, Boxo.

26
00:01:05,980 --> 00:01:08,392
I know, fair Lamas, I want some cool too.

27
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,000
This cold is just what the Boxo
ordered. Yeah, right? I know.

28
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:16,137
I'll wear that cloak Boxo got
me in the dark forest stratum.

29
00:01:16,220 --> 00:01:18,697
Not that she should need to use
another heat countermeasure,

30
00:01:18,780 --> 00:01:22,817
but Llamas is being nice and making it
a point to wear the cloak I gave her.

31
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:24,580
So, Boxo, how do I look?

32
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:26,200
Ad or a bo-oh.

33
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:28,320
Aw, thank you.

34
00:01:28,540 --> 00:01:32,246
It pays to compliment her when
she responds so, well, adorably.

35
00:01:32,420 --> 00:01:34,237
But it's no time for
soothing our discomfort.

36
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:39,202
We need to go to the Hunters Association
and deliver the letter from Director Bear.

37
00:01:45,380 --> 00:01:50,077
On the outside, I'm just a big metal box,
But inside I've still got a human soul!

38
00:01:50,160 --> 00:01:52,217
In this new world of
wonders I travel to and

39
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:54,777
fro on the back of my
super strong partner Lamas!

40
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:57,160
The name's Boxxo! Hello there!

41
00:01:57,500 --> 00:01:59,088
That means yes, by the way!

42
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:20,697
Unpunnyo yume nao Coin Shui ne?

43
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:23,157
Arwa ta eensho ni!

44
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:25,117
Splash sa sejai ba ii?

45
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:28,357
Atari ga te ta la mooi yippon.

46
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:31,137
Mirai wa kippo saita.

47
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:33,197
Amakubbe nihno.

48
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:35,597
Hjo mo hazikelu sa.

49
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:38,417
Diarmi movai te saita.

50
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:41,600
Sino saki no mabushimah Shui?

51
00:02:43,540 --> 00:02:46,660
Miichoku saita moono wa ddekein?

52
00:03:12,980 --> 00:03:15,697
We're here from the
Clear Flow Lake Stratum.

53
00:03:15,780 --> 00:03:17,837
We have a letter from the director there,

54
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:21,567
and we'd like to deliver it to
Director Scorching if we could.

55
00:03:22,880 --> 00:03:25,380
My word, Master Boxo, it can't be!

56
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:27,217
I haven't seen you in so long.

57
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:29,653
My sincerest apologies if I worried you.

58
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:30,660
Hello there.

59
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:32,980
Oh, Mishuel.

60
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:35,697
I did sort of forget
about him, to be honest.

61
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:36,960
Oops, my bad.

62
00:03:37,380 --> 00:03:40,357
Well, anyway, now I've caught up
with everyone who got scattered.

63
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:42,237
I got sent to this place by myself,

64
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:44,777
and as I was pondering how
I had no way to get back,

65
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:49,095
I ended up helping defend the village
when a swarm of monsters attacked.

66
00:03:50,060 --> 00:03:51,589
I'm glad that you're okay.

67
00:03:51,980 --> 00:03:55,297
Don't worry, everyone else is safe
back in the Clearflow Lake stratum.

68
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:56,737
Oh, I'm relieved to hear it.

69
00:03:56,820 --> 00:03:58,560
I'm glad we ran into Mishuel.

70
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:01,677
I wonder how he's been faring
on his own in this stratum.

71
00:04:01,760 --> 00:04:04,597
Here's hoping his communication
issues have improved a bit.

72
00:04:04,680 --> 00:04:06,757
It's such a relief you're here, Master.

73
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:10,837
All the stress and tension these past
few days have really wrecked my stomach.

74
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:11,750
Wrecked it!

75
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:13,997
It did nothing for your looks, either.

76
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:16,797
I guess there's no way you were
going to improve that quickly.

77
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:17,897
Thank you for waiting.

78
00:04:17,980 --> 00:04:20,215
The director says he will see you now.

79
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:22,677
Welcome, friends.

80
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:24,037
I'm glad you can make it.

81
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:26,697
Although this stratum has had
its own fair share of weirdness,

82
00:04:26,780 --> 00:04:29,177
what with the monster swarm
attacking the village and all,

83
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:32,017
we fought them all off, caught what
appeared to be their commander?

84
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:33,717
and threw their butts in jail.

85
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:35,153
Wow, that's impressive.

86
00:04:35,340 --> 00:04:38,693
So, um, we have a letter here
for you from Director Bear.

87
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:40,390
Huh.

88
00:04:40,540 --> 00:04:43,397
I see that you guys have
had it pretty rough as well.

89
00:04:43,480 --> 00:04:44,310
What?

90
00:04:44,393 --> 00:04:46,120
You can provide us with water? Yes.

91
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:48,500
That would be a big help.

92
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:51,877
This heat has the Oasis low on
water and things are looking bad.

93
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:53,437
Can I ask for it right away?

94
00:04:53,520 --> 00:04:54,400
Hello there.

95
00:04:55,100 --> 00:04:58,477
Since I started doing business on
this stratum with its horrible heat,

96
00:04:58,560 --> 00:05:01,497
the cold drinks have been flying
off the proverbial shelves.

97
00:05:01,580 --> 00:05:05,317
Been selling with no breaks from dawn
till dusk every day without fail.

98
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:07,900
Busy day, huh, Boxo? Yes.

99
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,306
What should we do after this?

100
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:11,917
Shooey's gone off somewhere.

101
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:12,830
Oh,

102
00:05:12,913 --> 00:05:16,177
do you maybe want to go check out the magic
item shop that was selling those boots?

103
00:05:16,260 --> 00:05:17,090
Good idea.

104
00:05:17,340 --> 00:05:19,377
Some sightseeing at night could be nice.

105
00:05:19,460 --> 00:05:20,290
Hello there.

106
00:05:21,740 --> 00:05:24,152
I wonder what kind of magic item this is.

107
00:05:24,620 --> 00:05:25,450
Ah,

108
00:05:25,533 --> 00:05:26,897
that one allows you to
clean your bathwater and

109
00:05:26,980 --> 00:05:29,157
store it in a bucket so
you can use it again.

110
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:31,217
Looks like Lamas is
going to do some shopping

111
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:33,737
before hitting up the
merchant for information.

112
00:05:33,820 --> 00:05:35,857
Wow, that would really come in handy.

113
00:05:35,940 --> 00:05:37,437
I'd like to buy it, please.

114
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:39,137
Oh, thank you for your business, miss.

115
00:05:39,220 --> 00:05:40,457
I've really been in luck lately.

116
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:43,117
You're the third new customer
who's coming today alone.

117
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:45,597
Would the others be a man
dressed like a clergyman

118
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:48,197
and a short-haired woman
with a bow on her back?

119
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:50,420
Oh, um, yes, as a matter of fact.

120
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:51,830
Why?

121
00:05:51,913 --> 00:05:52,743
Do you know them, miss?

122
00:05:52,826 --> 00:05:53,656
Mm-hmm.

123
00:05:53,739 --> 00:05:54,657
What did they have to say?

124
00:05:54,740 --> 00:05:56,740
Well, the clergyman had questions.

125
00:05:56,900 --> 00:05:59,137
He asked where I'd gotten
some boots I sold recently,

126
00:05:59,220 --> 00:06:02,220
then he left, but that
information is confidential.

127
00:06:02,380 --> 00:06:04,380
That was heavy, no doubt about it.

128
00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:08,337
Oh, sure, but would you mind telling me
which hunter sold you those boots, please?

129
00:06:08,420 --> 00:06:09,250
I'm sorry.

130
00:06:09,333 --> 00:06:11,077
I have to think of my reputation.

131
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:15,257
Looks like disclosure of personal info
is problematic even in this other world.

132
00:06:15,340 --> 00:06:18,780
In that case... Letter. What? Letter?

133
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:20,668
Oh, you mean those letters.

134
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:21,630
That's right.

135
00:06:21,713 --> 00:06:26,306
I've got letters of introduction from the
director here and one from Suori, too.

136
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:28,220
Hmm. Let's see.

137
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:30,477
This one's from Director
Scorching and what?

138
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:32,800
One from that giant corporation, too?

139
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:36,657
Suori's letter had an even bigger
effect than Director Scorching's?

140
00:06:36,740 --> 00:06:37,570
That's wild.

141
00:06:37,653 --> 00:06:39,377
Sawari calling herself the daughter of a

142
00:06:39,460 --> 00:06:41,777
big-time merchant might
be an understatement.

143
00:06:41,860 --> 00:06:44,157
I'll make an exception
and tell you this time.

144
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:47,637
There's no surviving in this business
if you cross those two, you know.

145
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:49,837
The salesman is scared out of her wits.

146
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:52,860
I'm very curious to know
what was in that letter.

147
00:06:53,380 --> 00:06:56,027
The one who sold the
boots to me was Tashtay,

148
00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:58,728
a hunter who's pretty
active on the stratum.

149
00:06:58,980 --> 00:06:59,810
Mr.

150
00:06:59,893 --> 00:07:03,557
Boxo, why couldn't you have invited me to
join you on your evening stroll tonight?

151
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:08,037
When I dine alone, women always end up
approaching me and it stresses me out!

152
00:07:08,120 --> 00:07:10,537
The fun thing about Mishuel
is that he's being sincere.

153
00:07:10,620 --> 00:07:12,257
I am being sarcastic, though.

154
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:16,877
Well, in any case, I asked Director
Scorching about this hunter called Tashtay.

155
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:20,377
Apparently, he's the leader of a hunter
team known as the Billowing Flames.

156
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:22,457
They number around a dozen in total.

157
00:07:22,540 --> 00:07:24,357
I was told they're
currently exploring some

158
00:07:24,440 --> 00:07:26,852
ruins in a desert region of this stratum.

159
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:28,280
Hello there!

160
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:31,157
If you wish to parlay with this Tashtay,

161
00:07:31,240 --> 00:07:33,557
then it seems your only option
is to make for the ruins.

162
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:37,737
But going there would mean having to
cross that awful desert, wouldn't it?

163
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:38,650
Hello there.

164
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:40,300
I thought so.

165
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:44,217
Oh, Master Boxo, would you mind
terribly if I accompanied you, please?

166
00:07:44,300 --> 00:07:47,157
I wish he wouldn't look at
me like an abandoned puppy.

167
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:49,181
I need to handle this skillfully.

168
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,920
I'll be to ask for you, Apprentice.

169
00:07:53,140 --> 00:07:55,316
Master Boxo called me his apprentice!

170
00:07:57,080 --> 00:07:58,197
Anything, you name it!

171
00:07:58,280 --> 00:07:59,110
Hold on!

172
00:07:59,193 --> 00:08:00,777
Are you planning to disappear again?

173
00:08:00,860 --> 00:08:03,557
Why are you trying to deal
with this all by yourself?

174
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:05,957
We have our issues, but
we're all on the same side.

175
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:07,457
This is a personal matter.

176
00:08:07,540 --> 00:08:09,417
I simply don't wish to inconvenience...

177
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:11,559
There you go, deciding on your own!

178
00:08:11,660 --> 00:08:13,248
Without even discussing it!

179
00:08:13,340 --> 00:08:14,693
Like Captain Carry Oil!

180
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:16,806
Now you're doing what he did!

181
00:08:17,180 --> 00:08:19,004
Maybe I'm just not trustworthy.

182
00:08:19,220 --> 00:08:20,520
He didn't talk to me.

183
00:08:20,780 --> 00:08:22,309
But if he had been honest,

184
00:08:22,460 --> 00:08:25,737
maybe these could have turned out
differently and we'd all be together.

185
00:08:25,820 --> 00:08:26,720
Aw, Shui.

186
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:29,449
So you all came here
in search of me, then.

187
00:08:29,580 --> 00:08:32,017
I am deeply sorry to have
caused you such trouble.

188
00:08:32,100 --> 00:08:35,517
If you think you've caused trouble,
then I want you to talk it out.

189
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:39,357
That's right, you leaving without
saying anything is what made us worry.

190
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:40,480
Yes, yes.

191
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:42,420
I think I understand.

192
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:47,197
I doubt you'll like this story,
but are you willing to hear it?

193
00:08:47,280 --> 00:08:48,110
Mm-hmm.

194
00:08:50,880 --> 00:08:54,174
It happened back before I
joined the Menagerie of Fools.

195
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:58,122
A childhood friend and I
were working as hunters.

196
00:08:58,620 --> 00:09:01,679
We knew each other well and
made an incredible team.

197
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:05,238
People were lauding us as
the next up-and-coming duo.

198
00:09:05,540 --> 00:09:07,600
So Heavy had a partner before.

199
00:09:07,980 --> 00:09:12,817
One day, after a series of lucky breaks,
I received a surprisingly hefty reward?

200
00:09:12,900 --> 00:09:16,297
and I decided to get my friend some
new boots for her upcoming birthday.

201
00:09:16,380 --> 00:09:19,420
Those boots were the untiring God's feet.

202
00:09:19,620 --> 00:09:22,057
The boots I won were the
same ones you gave her?

203
00:09:22,140 --> 00:09:23,340
Yes, that's right.

204
00:09:23,640 --> 00:09:26,540
She, my friend, was pleased with them too.

205
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:30,235
She wore those boots everywhere
she went, without fail.

206
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:33,137
She would always say she'd never
give them up no matter what,

207
00:09:33,220 --> 00:09:35,573
and she said it with a smile every time.

208
00:09:35,940 --> 00:09:37,940
Heavy's expression speaks volumes.

209
00:09:38,060 --> 00:09:41,317
There's no question how
important his friend was to him.

210
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:42,660
Not long after,

211
00:09:42,980 --> 00:09:46,477
we were attacked by bandits while
on assignment escorting a merchant,

212
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:49,760
and a blow from an adversary
left me unconscious.

213
00:09:51,260 --> 00:09:56,320
Once I came to, I was greeted by the
horrible sight of corpses all around me.

214
00:09:57,180 --> 00:10:02,420
There before my eyes were my friend's
remains, her legs cut off at the knees,

215
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:07,080
hewn off crudely, cruelly, with
an axe or other rough blade.

216
00:10:07,620 --> 00:10:08,720
My heart broke.

217
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:11,917
She had tied them too tightly
because they meant so much to her,

218
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,647
and the bandits couldn't
get them off of her.

219
00:10:14,880 --> 00:10:17,297
They wore masks so I
don't know their faces.

220
00:10:17,380 --> 00:10:20,145
My only clue was that
pair of boots they stole.

221
00:10:21,060 --> 00:10:22,720
And so, clinging to hope,

222
00:10:22,940 --> 00:10:27,017
I became obsessed with footwear,
single-minded in my quest for vengeance.

223
00:10:27,100 --> 00:10:28,337
That brings us to now.

224
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:31,655
I never expected Heavy to
have such a tragic hero past.

225
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:36,664
I may be a clergyman, but my heart has
been full of naught but revenge ever since.

226
00:10:36,940 --> 00:10:38,817
It's pathetic when you
consider the judgment

227
00:10:38,900 --> 00:10:41,457
I doled out to Captain
Kerioyl and his family.

228
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:42,400
You idiots!

229
00:10:42,720 --> 00:10:45,237
Both you and the captain,
you're total dumbasses!

230
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:46,817
If you had talked about it,

231
00:10:46,900 --> 00:10:49,537
we might have found the boots and
the people who sold them much sooner!

232
00:10:49,620 --> 00:10:51,677
If you had shared your own sad story,

233
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:54,037
they might have been willing to
talk about their family problems?

234
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:55,708
and we'd still be together.

235
00:10:56,060 --> 00:10:58,540
Yes, but this is my personal business.

236
00:10:58,880 --> 00:10:59,710
Don't you yes, but me.

237
00:10:59,793 --> 00:11:03,057
Can't you see things turned out this way
because everyone's so full of secrets?

238
00:11:03,140 --> 00:11:05,077
I'm sick of the lies and deception.

239
00:11:05,160 --> 00:11:06,377
It's really this simple.

240
00:11:06,460 --> 00:11:10,397
If you want help, all you have to do is
explain the situation and ask for help.

241
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:12,737
If it's too much or I don't
want to do it, I'll say.

242
00:11:12,820 --> 00:11:16,717
If what you're doing is wrong, as a
comrade, I'll do all I can to stop you.

243
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:20,997
So I wish you'd stop deciding and be a
burden or that you already know my answer.

244
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:22,280
It's infuriating.

245
00:11:27,080 --> 00:11:28,940
You're right. I was wrong.

246
00:11:29,300 --> 00:11:31,360
My fear made everything much worse.

247
00:11:31,680 --> 00:11:33,092
Thank you so much, Shui.

248
00:11:33,260 --> 00:11:34,090
I'm grateful.

249
00:11:34,173 --> 00:11:35,040
Don't sweat it.

250
00:11:35,220 --> 00:11:36,985
I'm just glad that you get it.

251
00:11:38,660 --> 00:11:41,140
Everyone, might I request your assistance?

252
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:43,700
The answer is obvious! Mm-hmm.

253
00:11:43,900 --> 00:11:45,077
I've got your back, friend.

254
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:47,737
At your service! Oh, fine. I'll help.

255
00:11:47,820 --> 00:11:48,760
If you insist.

256
00:11:49,540 --> 00:11:50,370
Hello there!

257
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:01,630
Huh?

258
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:03,130
All right.

259
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:06,657
Our first obstacle is finding a
way through the scorching desert.

260
00:12:06,740 --> 00:12:10,397
The environment is so harsh that even
walking through it will be difficult.

261
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:12,897
I wonder if that magic
item shop has anything

262
00:12:12,980 --> 00:12:14,857
that could maybe help
us deal with the heat.

263
00:12:14,940 --> 00:12:16,237
Sounds like you're in a bind.

264
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:17,797
When did you get here, Hulemy?

265
00:12:17,880 --> 00:12:18,710
Just now.

266
00:12:18,793 --> 00:12:20,137
I haven't had time to unpack.

267
00:12:20,220 --> 00:12:21,926
We wanted to come along, too!

268
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:27,335
Are you going to be okay in this heat?

269
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:31,237
I may be a snow fairy, but I'm not
going to melt if it gets too hot.

270
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:34,026
Besides, I can cool down
the air if I need to.

271
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:37,677
As for the temperature problem,
I have a solution for that.

272
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:41,697
This magic item has the effect of
blocking heat and cooling nearby moisture.

273
00:12:41,780 --> 00:12:45,097
It'll turn any sweat and
humidity into a refreshing mist.

274
00:12:45,180 --> 00:12:46,239
Simply incredible.

275
00:12:46,540 --> 00:12:49,857
With that item, I bet we'd be able
to cross the desert with ease.

276
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:51,437
Also, these are for Lamas.

277
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:54,461
They're from the Dark
Forest Stratum weapons shop.

278
00:12:54,980 --> 00:12:57,617
Apparently, they can
somehow change their weight.

279
00:12:57,700 --> 00:12:58,530
Amazing!

280
00:12:58,640 --> 00:13:01,137
Those will make her attacks
way stronger and help

281
00:13:01,220 --> 00:13:04,044
her maintain control when
she's going full tilt.

282
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:06,475
All right, I'm not as worried anymore.

283
00:13:07,680 --> 00:13:10,800
I seem to have caused
quite the kerfuffle. Yes!

284
00:13:11,580 --> 00:13:14,462
Truth be told, I never
planned on telling anyone.

285
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:17,598
But I suppose I ought to think Shui.

286
00:13:17,740 --> 00:13:18,977
It can't have been easy,

287
00:13:19,060 --> 00:13:23,297
but at least now he's able to unload some
of the burdens he's had to carry alone.

288
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:25,477
I'm not naive enough to
think that everything

289
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:27,617
will be resolved during this one outing,

290
00:13:27,700 --> 00:13:29,876
but maybe I'll find a stopping point.

291
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:32,620
I hope it works out.

292
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:34,440
So do I.

293
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:38,460
It's as hot as we expected.

294
00:13:38,780 --> 00:13:40,251
No, even hotter, I'd say.

295
00:13:40,440 --> 00:13:42,737
Even though we're wearing the
cloaks Hulemy made for us,

296
00:13:42,820 --> 00:13:45,173
it seems to be tough going for everyone.

297
00:13:45,340 --> 00:13:47,117
We'll scratch that, not everyone.

298
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:50,318
Just a little farther, guys,
then we'll take a break.

299
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:52,404
Lamas and Botan are doing fine.

300
00:13:52,640 --> 00:13:56,157
Thanks to my temperature regulation
powers, Llamas isn't sweating at all.

301
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:59,887
And Botan seems dandy with all
the cold air Kiko is providing.

302
00:14:02,060 --> 00:14:03,120
You're so cold.

303
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:07,037
If you could be my boyfriend for
just this stratum, that'd be amazing.

304
00:14:07,120 --> 00:14:08,937
I'd even settle for being best friends.

305
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:09,850
Come now, you two.

306
00:14:09,933 --> 00:14:10,763
He's my master.

307
00:14:11,240 --> 00:14:13,477
Boxxo is looking more and more attractive.

308
00:14:13,560 --> 00:14:15,717
Honestly, you could just
have me at this point.

309
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:18,117
Oh, master, I'd do anything, you ask me.

310
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:21,494
Now that I look close, his
body is like a pair of boots.

311
00:14:21,900 --> 00:14:22,980
Snap out of it.

312
00:14:23,200 --> 00:14:26,082
The more you three talk,
the less sense you make.

313
00:14:33,820 --> 00:14:35,217
Ah, this is happening.

314
00:14:35,300 --> 00:14:36,440
I feel alive again.

315
00:14:36,780 --> 00:14:38,400
Leave it to Master Boxo.

316
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:41,337
I didn't expect the heat to
be too much for the clothes.

317
00:14:41,420 --> 00:14:42,837
It's not like they were useless.

318
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:44,757
When I took mine off, it was so hot,

319
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:48,134
I thought I was going to
shrivel up and die right there.

320
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:51,070
Hmm?

321
00:14:51,180 --> 00:14:54,298
Is that some sort of calendar
they use in this world?

322
00:14:54,600 --> 00:14:55,430
Calendar?

323
00:14:55,620 --> 00:14:56,450
What was that?

324
00:14:56,580 --> 00:14:58,340
Did you say something, Boxo?

325
00:14:58,540 --> 00:14:59,658
Is that a calendar?

326
00:14:59,820 --> 00:15:01,996
Those numbers are dates, aren't they?

327
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:03,900
Yeah, that's exactly it.

328
00:15:04,220 --> 00:15:06,717
Since we had a moment, I
wanted to check today's date.

329
00:15:06,800 --> 00:15:07,630
Hmm.

330
00:15:07,713 --> 00:15:09,597
Oh, one of the dates is circled in red.

331
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:10,510
Uh-huh.

332
00:15:10,720 --> 00:15:12,544
It marks a certain anniversary.

333
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:14,320
Got it.

334
00:15:14,540 --> 00:15:15,717
I'll leave it at that.

335
00:15:15,800 --> 00:15:18,212
I shouldn't pry into her private affairs.

336
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:21,797
Whoa that's the desert pillar.

337
00:15:21,880 --> 00:15:26,197
Yep the desert pillar is supposed to
be huge so it's likely still far off.

338
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:29,897
Desert pillar is apparently another
name for the ruins of an old tower.

339
00:15:29,980 --> 00:15:33,057
It's said to be a hundred
stories tall and the

340
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:35,964
stratum lord can be found
on the very top floor.

341
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:42,797
His black feathers look striking
against the cloudless sky.

342
00:15:42,880 --> 00:15:44,860
Wait what? Kuroyata!

343
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:47,217
They say you saw him disappear, too.

344
00:15:47,300 --> 00:15:48,917
Yeah, he vanished into thin air.

345
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,412
Good to know I wasn't just seeing things.

346
00:15:53,860 --> 00:15:55,160
I don't see anything.

347
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:56,957
I was sure this was the spot, though.

348
00:15:57,040 --> 00:16:00,240
Wait, something seems
kind of weird here. Huh?

349
00:16:00,680 --> 00:16:02,580
Whoa, Lamas. What's going on?

350
00:16:02,800 --> 00:16:04,271
The tower's really close.

351
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:06,402
It's right there in front of us.

352
00:16:07,820 --> 00:16:08,650
Huh?

353
00:16:08,733 --> 00:16:10,418
Why are you looking at me like that?

354
00:16:11,820 --> 00:16:15,644
I never would have guessed the
desert pillar would be this close.

355
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:21,157
It looks like there's some kind of illusion
magic at work, similar to my blessing.

356
00:16:21,240 --> 00:16:25,237
That makes sense, Kuroyata disappeared
after flying past that point.

357
00:16:25,320 --> 00:16:27,577
Which was making us misjudge the distance.

358
00:16:27,660 --> 00:16:32,601
I'm betting this trick was set up on purpose,
to keep anyone from getting too close.

359
00:16:33,300 --> 00:16:34,130
Kuroyata!

360
00:16:37,300 --> 00:16:38,240
Thank goodness

361
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:40,030
Yes.

362
00:16:40,113 --> 00:16:40,943
Let's see.

363
00:16:41,026 --> 00:16:42,697
He said there were a bunch of
what seemed to be lookouts,

364
00:16:42,780 --> 00:16:45,157
but they went inside to get
arrows when they spotted him,

365
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:46,897
so this would be a good time to go in.

366
00:16:46,980 --> 00:16:50,921
We can't afford to pass up this
chance that Kuroyata set up for us.

367
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:55,560
One and two!

368
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:01,660
It's cold in here.

369
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:04,150
Monster!

370
00:17:04,233 --> 00:17:05,063
It's enormous!

371
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:06,877
But something's wrong.

372
00:17:06,960 --> 00:17:08,157
Why aren't they reacting?

373
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:09,957
They look like they're
waiting for instructions

374
00:17:10,040 --> 00:17:12,877
but the commander here
has already been captured.

375
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:15,917
That makes sense it lines
up with what director

376
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:18,817
scorching told us maybe
the commander is a fake.

377
00:17:18,900 --> 00:17:21,077
To make us lower our
guard while they build up

378
00:17:21,160 --> 00:17:23,397
their forces and make plans
to attack the village.

379
00:17:23,480 --> 00:17:26,557
That would certainly
explain this situation wait

380
00:17:26,640 --> 00:17:28,697
a sec i just thought of a
way to turn this around.

381
00:17:28,780 --> 00:17:32,297
On him here goes nothing

382
00:17:32,380 --> 00:17:39,380
nice

383
00:17:44,780 --> 00:17:45,610
the

384
00:17:45,693 --> 00:17:47,177
plan's working heavy's using his

385
00:17:47,260 --> 00:17:51,084
illusions to make These monsters
think that their buddies are us.

386
00:17:56,100 --> 00:17:58,747
Time to take this new
gear out on a test run.

387
00:17:59,240 --> 00:18:01,220
Let's start by getting heavier.

388
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:04,400
I did it!

389
00:18:04,600 --> 00:18:06,482
That was surprisingly effective.

390
00:18:12,700 --> 00:18:16,524
It looks like Field will be able
to save up quite a bit of power.

391
00:18:17,060 --> 00:18:18,580
That was the easy part.

392
00:18:19,140 --> 00:18:22,697
Now we've got to deal with any
ambushes or traps waiting ahead.

393
00:18:22,780 --> 00:18:24,377
Voxo, do you think you could go in front?

394
00:18:24,460 --> 00:18:26,977
Your barrier is probably
going to come in handy here.

395
00:18:27,060 --> 00:18:27,980
Yes, yes.

396
00:18:28,420 --> 00:18:31,000
I'll be right there with you. Hey, sorry.

397
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:33,837
I don't mean to interrupt
while you're making plans.

398
00:18:33,920 --> 00:18:35,837
But do you think I could have seconds?

399
00:18:35,920 --> 00:18:37,449
I've still got a back-ish.

400
00:18:40,200 --> 00:18:43,259
Voxo, be ready for anything
from this point forward.

401
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:44,440
Hello there.

402
00:18:45,340 --> 00:18:46,170
Let's go.

403
00:18:56,220 --> 00:18:57,740
All right, we made it!

404
00:18:58,560 --> 00:19:00,580
Everyone, you can come up now!

405
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:06,442
Is something the matter, Hulemy?

406
00:19:06,540 --> 00:19:10,357
I was just thinking that if whoever set
these traps knew what we were doing to them,

407
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:11,675
they'd be pretty mad.

408
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:12,760
For sure.

409
00:19:13,020 --> 00:19:15,577
If it were me, I don't
know if I could handle it.

410
00:19:15,660 --> 00:19:18,497
It appears there are enemies
waiting beyond the door.

411
00:19:18,580 --> 00:19:19,410
Right.

412
00:19:19,493 --> 00:19:22,340
Llamas, go ahead and
bust it wide open. Yeah!

413
00:19:22,820 --> 00:19:23,660
Knock, knock!

414
00:19:26,260 --> 00:19:28,037
Looks like they were
lurking behind the door

415
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:30,297
so they could pounce on
us the second it opened.

416
00:19:30,380 --> 00:19:32,674
They definitely weren't expecting that.

417
00:19:33,900 --> 00:19:35,900
They must be the Billowing Flames.

418
00:19:37,260 --> 00:19:40,540
Who the hell do you guys
think you are? That man.

419
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:43,457
He matches the description
we were given for Tashtay.

420
00:19:43,540 --> 00:19:44,370
It's him.

421
00:19:44,453 --> 00:19:45,283
There's no doubt about it.

422
00:19:45,366 --> 00:19:49,197
We're a group of hunters who came
here from the Clearflow Lake Stratum.

423
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:51,162
So, you're from another stratum.

424
00:19:51,280 --> 00:19:52,692
What are you doing here?

425
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:57,821
If you must know, the reason we came is to
discuss some important business with you.

426
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:01,000
But we received more of a
welcome than we expected.

427
00:20:01,940 --> 00:20:03,469
You want to talk business?

428
00:20:03,760 --> 00:20:06,257
You're going to tell us how
the hell you found out that we

429
00:20:06,340 --> 00:20:09,377
were hiding monsters in here
so we could attack the village?

430
00:20:09,460 --> 00:20:11,989
Sure enough, that was
their plan all along.

431
00:20:12,380 --> 00:20:15,909
First, I'd appreciate it if you
cleared something up for me.

432
00:20:16,420 --> 00:20:17,250
Huh?

433
00:20:17,333 --> 00:20:20,077
Your group has been conspiring
with the Netherlord.

434
00:20:20,160 --> 00:20:21,977
And that's the reason why you've been able

435
00:20:22,060 --> 00:20:24,417
to control the monsters
on the first floor.

436
00:20:24,500 --> 00:20:26,757
Does that just about sum everything up?

437
00:20:26,840 --> 00:20:28,597
If you already know that much,

438
00:20:28,680 --> 00:20:31,377
then I suppose there's no
point in trying to play dumb.

439
00:20:31,460 --> 00:20:34,857
Yeah, it's only temporary, but
we're working with the Netherlord.

440
00:20:34,940 --> 00:20:37,117
But why are you on the Demon Lord's side?

441
00:20:37,200 --> 00:20:38,737
You're only hurting innocent people!

442
00:20:38,820 --> 00:20:39,900
Yeah, yeah.

443
00:20:40,260 --> 00:20:42,637
You could spare me all
that goody-two-shoes talk.

444
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:44,377
We're doing it for money, of course.

445
00:20:44,460 --> 00:20:48,377
It's a no-brainer when we're getting enough
money that we never have to work again.

446
00:20:48,460 --> 00:20:49,677
From the way you're talking,

447
00:20:49,760 --> 00:20:51,177
it sounds as if you're quite comfortable

448
00:20:51,260 --> 00:20:53,848
with doing illegal
things for personal gain.

449
00:20:54,260 --> 00:20:55,672
Got a problem with that?

450
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:57,697
Robberies, rapes, and even murder.

451
00:20:57,780 --> 00:20:59,956
It all blends together after a while.

452
00:21:00,060 --> 00:21:02,413
What do you expect from a former bandit?

453
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:03,750
Believe me,

454
00:21:03,833 --> 00:21:05,597
there's nothing that feels
better than trampling

455
00:21:05,680 --> 00:21:07,677
over a weakling while they beg for mercy.

456
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:09,160
Isn't that right, boys?

457
00:21:09,260 --> 00:21:10,260
It's the best!

458
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:12,300
These guys are total scum!

459
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:13,660
As I suspected.

460
00:21:14,460 --> 00:21:17,342
Well, in that case, do
you recognize these boots?

461
00:21:18,100 --> 00:21:19,806
What are they supposed to be?

462
00:21:20,140 --> 00:21:21,100
Hold on, boss.

463
00:21:21,260 --> 00:21:24,966
Aren't those the boots we sold
for a pretty penny a while back?

464
00:21:25,660 --> 00:21:26,490
That's right.

465
00:21:26,573 --> 00:21:28,197
I stole them off of that hunter.

466
00:21:28,280 --> 00:21:29,440
I remember now.

467
00:21:29,820 --> 00:21:32,717
That chick was going on about
how she'd never hand them over

468
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:36,137
no matter what because she got
them from someone dear to her.

469
00:21:36,220 --> 00:21:39,455
She was pissing me off, so
I cut off her freaking legs.

470
00:21:39,800 --> 00:21:40,860
Oh, I see.

471
00:21:41,360 --> 00:21:42,460
What a treat.

472
00:21:44,020 --> 00:21:46,340
At last, I get to achieve my goal.

473
00:21:46,760 --> 00:21:51,160
I've prayed for this moment countless
times, and now it's finally here.

474
00:21:51,540 --> 00:21:54,640
You have no idea how
I've longed to find you.

475
00:21:54,960 --> 00:21:56,784
You may beg me for forgiveness.

476
00:21:57,300 --> 00:21:59,280
You may cry from the pain.

477
00:22:00,500 --> 00:22:04,580
You may even attempt to repent,
but none of it will save you.

478
00:23:37,720 --> 00:23:39,838
I look forward to serving you again.
